                <pb facs="0824" n="810" xml:id="pg810"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Barlow, United States marshal, to Mr. Fish,
                        Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-07-15"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 15,
                        1809</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>:</p>
                <p>Authorization received. Some two hundred persons are on Gardner’s Island. They
                    refuse to leave on the request of my officers and the cutter. They have robbed
                    the light-house keeper. I must send down a sufficient force to oblige them to
                    leave. I shall act very discreetly. If I cannot get enough marines may I ask for
                    a few troops?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FRANCIS C. BARLOW,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States
                            Marshal.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
